title: Found Things
id: found
tab: 13 · Found Things
about: 13 · The finale: the Found Things thank whoever left them behind
lead: tabby
key: D
bpm: 92
bass: none
backing: neon +0, watt +2, cue +4, clank +0, zap +4
finale: "Belong" = 1 0/3

# Verse voices in stage order: Watt sings Spool, Tabby and Gruff sing themselves, and Neon sings Clacker.
tune a = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4 5 4 2 4/2 | I 4, VI 4
tune b = 4 5/.5 7/.5 7 5 4 2 1/2 | IV 4, V 4

[verse 1]
rest 8
watt: "I was a tape left in a drawer" = a ; do nod ; move left 4 ; cam two-shot
tabby: "I was a screen that lost its glow" = a ; do nod ; take walk-right ; move right 4 ; cam two-shot
gruff: "I was a tangle left for dead" = a ; do shrug ; take toaster-shrug ; move wide-left 4 ; cam closeup
neon: "I was the keys by the back door" = b ; do nod ; take walk ; move wide-right 4 ; cam wide

[chorus, choir]
"We are the found things put to use" = 4/.5 4/.5 5 7 7 5 4 2/2 | I 4, V 4 ; do cheer ; dance 6 ; cam wide
  + chip: "We are the found things put to use" = 6/.5 6/.5 7 9 9 7 6 4/2 ; take action
  + gruff: "We are the found things put to use" = 2/.5 2/.5 3 5 5 3 2 0/2 ; move center 4
"Built from the bits that you let loose" = 2 2/.5 4/.5 5 5 4 2 1/2 | VI 4, V 4 ; move center 4 ; cam two-shot
  + chip: "Built from the bits that you let loose" = 4 4/.5 6/.5 7 7 6 4 3/2 ; move left 4
  + gruff: "Built from the bits that you let loose" = 0 0/.5 2/.5 3 3 2 0 -1/2 ; dance 4
"Thank you for all you left behind" = 4/.5 4/.5 5 7 8 7 5 4/2 | IV 4, I 4 ; jump 1.5 ; cam low-angle
  + chip: "Thank you for all you left behind" = 6/.5 6/.5 7 9 10 9 7 6/2 ; take stamp
  + gruff: "Thank you for all you left behind" = 2/.5 2/.5 3 5 6 5 3 2/2 ; move left 4
"At four oh four we all belong" = 4 5/.5 4/.5 2 1 2 1 0/2 | II 4, V 2, I 2 ; do bow ; celebrate 4 ; cam wide
  + chip: "At four oh four we all belong" = 6 7/.5 6/.5 4 3 4 3 2/2 ; move center 4
  + gruff: "At four oh four we all belong" = 2 3/.5 2/.5 0 -1 0 -1 0/2 ; celebrate 4

[verse 2]
watt: "I kept a tape of one last show" = a ; do tilt ; move right 4 ; cam two-shot
tabby: "I had a voice I kept inside" = a ; do nod ; take toast ; move left 4 ; cam closeup
gruff: "I felt a tug along my wire" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4 5 4 2 4 4 | I 4, VI 4 ; do nod ; move right 4 ; cam reaction
neon: "I knew one chord from that old show" = b ; do laugh ; take alt-idle ; move left 4 ; cam wide

[repeat chorus]

[verse 3]
watt: "I found the show. I pressed rewind" = a ; do cheer ; jump 1.5 ; move left 4 ; cam two-shot
tabby: "I heard the tune and sang along" = a ; do laugh ; move wide-right 4 ; cam reaction
gruff: "I plucked my string. The floor hummed too" = a ; do nod ; move wide-left 4 ; cam low-angle
neon: "I played that chord. You knew it too" = b ; do nod ; take walk ; move center 4 ; cam wide

[repeat chorus]

[bridge]
folio: "You closed the book and dimmed the light" = 5/.5 5/.5 7 5 4 5 4 3/2 | VI 4, IV 4 ; do tilt ; take chuckle ; move left 4 ; cam closeup
neon: "You left us waiting in the dark" = 4/.5 4/.5 5 4 2 3 4 5/2 | VI 4, IV 4 ; do nod ; take alt-idle ; move center 4 ; cam two-shot
tabby: "You gave us more than you could know" = 5/.5 4/.5 3 2 1 3 5 7/2 | II 4, IV 4 ; do nod ; move left 4 ; cam closeup
chip: "Now hear the song we saved for you" = 3/.5 4/.5 5 7 5 4 5 6/2 | IV 4, V 4 ; do cheer ; take action ; jump 1.5 ; cam low-angle
  + folio @4: "saved for you" = 6 7 8/2 ; do cheer ; take belt ; celebrate 4

[repeat chorus]
